proxmox-kernel-7.3 (7.3.6-1+s390x7) trixie; urgency=medium

  * KVM: s390: ESA/390 DAT shadowing: purge the guest TLB when the vCPU
    switches to another shadow address space.
  * KVM: s390: let user space inject the external interruptions it
    emulates and exit to user space when such an interruption can be
    presented (capability KVM_CAP_S390_USER_EXT_IRQ); with a selftest.
  * KVM: s390: on hosts without the CZAM facility (z196, z114, zEC12,
    zBC12) let the ESA/390-compatibility mode use the machine's own DAT;
    no change on newer machines.
  * Interim build: the binary packages were built incrementally in the
    build tree of 7.3.6-1+s390x6 (only the changed objects rebuilt); a
    later version will be a clean build from this source.

 -- Yvan Janssens <yvanj@cyber.gent>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 19:28:10 +0000

proxmox-kernel-7.3 (7.3.6-1+s390x6) trixie; urgency=medium

  * KVM: s390: ESA/390-compatibility mode for first-level guests
    (capability KVM_CAP_S390_ESA390_CM, VM attribute
    KVM_S390_VM_ARCH_MODE) and ESA/390 DAT shadowing (flag
    KVM_S390_ESA390_CM_DAT): guests that IPL in ESA/390 can run under
    KVM, including with dynamic address translation in the primary
    space; with selftests. Opt-in per VM, no change for other guests.

 -- Yvan Janssens <yvanj@cyber.gent>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:20:47 +0000

proxmox-kernel-7.3 (7.3.6-1+s390x5) trixie; urgency=medium

  * s390x: enable legacy ebtables (ebtables module with the filter, nat
    and broute tables), which the Proxmox VE firewall uses for bridged
    guest traffic; the same setting as on amd64 and arm64.

 -- Yvan Janssens <yvanj@cyber.gent>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 11:30:50 +0000

